nd I have a nice in  the past you only do it with piano now I  have very good pianist still but I have  a drummer and a bass player world-class  musicians and it's really fun singing  with them and the bassist just so good I  do this song called all the love I have  which is from Angela Webb errs the  beautiful game and there's a little  break in it and the bass player does  this little musical break where he plays  like the melody of the song and it's  just so gorgeous I love it the first  time I rehearsed with the band and he  played that I turned around I was like  that is so beautiful so I'm glad I was  like I have to fly all three of those  musicians and put them up and pay them  to come to Oregon with me because  they're all so wonderful yeah it's gonna  be great playing your hometown as well  I'm guessing yeah Springfield Oregon if  anybody's on the west coast or near  Oregon I'd recommend you come it's at  the Wildish Theatre in Springfield  Oregon wildest theatre com-pub when's it  gonna be on July 13th yeah I just came  back to bones briefly oh you're kind of  favorite moments and scenes that you  played over the years or maybe your  favorite memories when you were off set  as well off screen with friends in the  show well my favorite episode was the  first year's Christmas episode the man  in the fallout shelter where we were all  trapped in the lab I had a lot of fun  with that that was we really got to all  work together more often than in the  other episodes because it was just us  and maybe my favorite scene ever though  was I think it was second season where I  punched Hodgins that was fun  that was a really really fun scene I  enjoyed that so and then off-camera  it's been fun even still hanging out  with the cast even after I've left the  show there's art cg2 I think that's  amazing  TJ thein who plays Hodgins actually went  to Paris with me last fall and we signed  autographs of Paris manga there which  was great other fun things with the cast  an